{"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSToolBarTop","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents14OUDSToolBarTopV","roleHeading":"Structure","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","name":"iOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","name":"iPadOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","name":"Mac Catalyst","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","name":"visionOS","beta":false}],"title":"OUDSToolBarTop","modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OUDSToolBarTop","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The top toolbar (aka "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"navigation bar"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on iOS and iPadOS 18 and lower) sits at the top of the screen and provides contextual information"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and controls related to the current view."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It typically displays the page title, and may include navigation actions such as “Back” or “Close” as well as supplementary actions."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It can contain leading, principal (center, single item only), and trailing actions."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop\/init(title:hasLargeTitle:subtitle:leadingItems:principalItem:trailingItems:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop\/body(content:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop\/ViewModifier-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSToolBarTop","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Warning","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": If an item is placed in principal position, the subtitle is never displayed (whatever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasLargeTitle"},{"type":"text","text":" is), because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".principal"},{"type":"text","text":" placement only replaces the inline compact bar title, not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".navigationSubtitle()"},{"type":"text","text":" (iOS 26+), which would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise keep rendering next to the item with no visible title next to it. The title itself is displayed only if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasLargeTitle"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" (in that case it appears below the bar, in large title mode, not inside it)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Appearances","type":"heading","anchor":"Appearances"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With Liquid Glass \/ iOS 26+ the OS will change the rendering of the toolbar items depending to the context:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The OS can group the items of same types in one group with kind of rectangle (e.g. views with menus)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"But for buttons items they will remain isolated","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The placement of the title can be leading or centered depending to the length of the text","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The text can be truncated if there is not enough remaining space","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The OS can apply another style for the back button","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without Liquid Glass \/ iOS 18 and lower, the OS won’t change that much the style of the toolbar items, Items won’t be visually grouped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The appearance of navigation bar elements is changed by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"oudsNavigationBarAppearance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" helper, which must be applied to the root view of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Technical constraints","type":"heading","anchor":"Technical-constraints"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To ensure the back button and text use the correct color on iOS 18 and earlier, apply the following accent color in your main view:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    struct AppMainView: View {","        var body: some View {","            ContentView()","                .accentColor(theme.colors.contentDefault)","        }","    }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Platform considerations","type":"heading","anchor":"Platform-considerations"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is available on iOS, iPadOS, and visionOS","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is not available for watchOS, tvOS and macOS","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":2,"text":"Badges uses","type":"heading","anchor":"Badges-uses"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For iOS 26 with Liquid Glass, the system badge is used because the OUDS badge component does not provide a suitable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rendering with the glassified effect applied on the top toolbar."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For iOS until 18 and without Liquid Glass  OUDS badge component is always used."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Code sample","type":"heading","anchor":"Code-sample"},{"code":["    ContentView()","        .toolBarTop(\"Title\",","            leadingItems: {","                OUDSToolBarItem(navigation: .back())","            },","            principalItem: OUDSToolBarItem(icon: Image(decorative: \"search\"), accessibilityLabel: \"Search\") { \/* Action to process *\/ },","            trailingItems: {","                OUDSToolBarItem(label: \"Label\") { \/* Action to process *\/ }","                OUDSToolBarItem(icon: Image(decorative: \"some_image\"), accessibilityLabel: \"Label\") { \/* Action to process *\/ }","            }","        )"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" helper can also be used to apply a SwiftUI toolbar configuration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    toolBarTop(_:hasLargeTitle:subtitle:leadingItems:principalItem:trailingItems:)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Design documentation","type":"heading","anchor":"Design-documentation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-ios-tool-bar-top"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Themes rendering","type":"heading","anchor":"Themes-rendering"},{"level":3,"text":"Liquid Glass","type":"heading","anchor":"Liquid-Glass"},{"level":4,"t